WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.925
Phase 3, general rollout, repeats the proven
pattern until every division has moved.

2
00:00:05.925 --> 00:00:09.478
A wave is a set of divisions
chosen by attribute value,

3
00:00:09.478 --> 00:00:12.950
usually by region, with the
lowest-risk region first.

4
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.017
Group Policy links stay
in place during a wave,

5
00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:20.538
and come off a migrated OU only
after seven days of clean compliance.

6
00:00:20.538 --> 00:00:23.415
The sponsor and steering
committee clear G3

7
00:00:23.415 --> 00:00:26.525
when every division has
passed its own exit gate.

8
00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:30.650
Then the work changes character:
these phases take old things away.

9
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:36.122
Phase 4 retires AD FS, user and device
certificate issuance from AD CS,

10
00:00:36.122 --> 00:00:38.907
DNS forwarders, Group Policy links,

11
00:00:38.907 --> 00:00:44.187
non-essential trusts and legacy
servers, each through its own plan.

12
00:00:44.187 --> 00:00:47.976
A component is retired only
while its rollback still works.

13
00:00:47.976 --> 00:00:53.013
Some things stay until the domain itself
retires: its own DNS zones, the domain

14
00:00:53.013 --> 00:00:58.050
controller and LDAPS certificates, and
the default domain account policies.

15
00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.975
The steward clears G4.

16
00:00:59.975 --> 00:01:04.747
Phase 5 retires AD DS itself, which
the master plan never reached,

17
00:01:04.747 --> 00:01:09.338
or reduces it to a documented
Kerberos island with an end date.

18
00:01:09.338 --> 00:01:11.326
Two steps are easy to forget.

19
00:01:11.326 --> 00:01:13.162
Records come before hardware.

20
00:01:13.162 --> 00:01:17.297
And domain controllers store the
password hashes of every account,

21
00:01:17.297 --> 00:01:20.324
so retired hosts and their
storage are sanitized.

22
00:01:20.324 --> 00:01:25.575
The sponsor and CIO clear G5, and they
decide when each component retires,

23
00:01:25.575 --> 00:01:28.510
after the records officer is consulted.
